# The web image builds from the repository root, so everything here is context
# that would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon and then thrown away.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters: it is platform-specific, the image
# installs its own, and sending it makes the build minutes slower for nothing.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own.
apps/web/build
apps/web/.svelte-kit

# .NET — the API image has its own context and its own ignore file.
**/bin
**/obj

.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
.playwright
.impeccable
**/.impeccable

# Documentation and screenshots: 3 MB of PNG that never reaches the image.
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Never. `.env` holds the pairing code and the database password.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/.env
